Privacy Policy

KANRIN CO., LTD. (hereinafter referred to as "the Company") recognizes the importance of personal information of registered users and is committed to complying with laws and regulations regarding the protection of personal information. The Company will strive to handle and manage personal information appropriately as described below. The Company will ensure the accuracy of personal information and manage it securely. When providing personal information to the Company, users are requested to provide their information after agreeing to the following contents.

Article 1 (Acquisition of Personal Information)
    The Company acquires personal information through the following methods:
    (1) Methods of directly receiving provision of personal information from users.
    (2) Methods of automatically recording personal information when users use the Company's services.
    (3) Methods of indirectly receiving provision of users' personal information from third parties.
    (4) Methods of acquiring personal information published in publications, on the Internet, etc.

    The personal information acquired is as follows:
    (1) User's basic information (address, name, gender, date of birth, nationality, passport number, email address, telephone number, mailing address, etc.)
    (2) User's additional information (occupation, workplace (company name, address, telephone number, department, job title, etc.))
    (3) Payment information (credit card number, bank account, invoice/receipt destination, etc.)
    (4) Information related to the use of services provided by the Company (history, purchase information, etc.)
    (5) Contents of communications sent from the user to the Company (emails, form input contents, etc.)
    (6) Information automatically collected in this service (Cookies, IP address, etc.)
    The above includes attribute information that does not itself constitute personal information (e.g., age, gender, occupation, area of residence), Cookies, and IP addresses (hereinafter collectively referred to as "Associated Information"). However, if a user provides personal information to the Company when using the Company's services, such information may be linked with the Associated Information, in which case the said Associated Information will also be treated as personal information.

    The provision of personal information by users is voluntary. However, if required items necessary for the Company's services are not entered, the Company may not be able to fully provide all or part of its services.

Article 2 (Use of Personal Information)
The Company will use users' personal information for the following purposes. Except as provided by laws and regulations or unless the purpose of use is separately indicated, the Company will not use personal information for any other purposes.
(1) Operation and management of services operated by the Company.
(2) Payment, settlement, billing, refunds, receipt issuance, and other operations related to accounting for services provided by the Company.
(3) Investigation and response in the event of failures, malfunctions, or accidents in the Company's systems, networks, etc.; measures necessary for the secure operation of the Company's services.
(4) Improvement and new development of the Company's services.
(5) Proposal of various services, provision of information, and delivery of advertisements to users.
(6) Communication and provision of information in relation to transactions with the Company's business partners and other transactions.
(7) Survey and analysis of service usage status and marketing.

Article 3 (Provision of Personal Information to Third Parties)
The Company will not provide personally identifiable information (name, address, telephone number, email address, etc.) to third parties without prior consent of the individual, except as set forth in the following items. Please note that the provision of users' personal information to companies, schools, organizations, etc., with which the Company has necessary partnerships or contractual relationships in providing services, shall not be deemed as disclosure or provision to third parties under this Article.
(1) When there is consent from the user.
(2) When based on laws and regulations.
(3) When necessary to protect the life, body, or property of an individual and it is difficult to obtain the consent of the user.
(4) When particularly necessary for improving public health or promoting the sound growth of children and it is difficult to obtain the consent of the user.
(5) When necessary to cooperate with a state institution, a local public body, or a person entrusted by them in executing affairs prescribed by laws and regulations, and obtaining the consent of the user is likely to impede the execution of such affairs.
(6) When disclosing or providing information processed to a degree where the individual cannot be identified.
(7) When provided in connection with business succession due to merger, company split, business transfer, or other reasons.

Article 4 (Outsourcing)
Notwithstanding the provisions of the preceding article, the Company may outsource part of its business in providing services to users and may provide users' personal information to outsourcing recipients within and outside Japan to the extent necessary for achieving the purposes of use. In such cases, the Company will conduct a rigorous investigation of the third party, take necessary and appropriate measures in accordance with the laws and regulations of the transferring and receiving countries, and exercise necessary and appropriate supervision to ensure confidentiality is maintained.
Note: The original Japanese text lacks specific details regarding the legal basis for international data transfers, which may be required under Japanese law (e.g., obtaining user consent or ensuring the recipient country has an adequate data protection framework). It is recommended to clarify this point.

Article 5 (Disclosure, Correction, Suspension of Use, and Deletion of Personal Information)
If the Company receives a request from the user for any of the following, it will promptly respond in accordance with the procedures established by the Company, except as provided by law. However, the Company may refuse such requests if they interfere with the Company's business operations or if the request is for disclosure of information other than the individual's personal information.
(1) Notification of the purpose of use of personal information.
(2) Disclosure of personal information held by the Company.
(3) Correction, addition, or deletion of the content of personal information (based on the reason that the content of the personal information differs from the facts).
(4) Cessation of provision of personal information to third parties (based on the reason that personal information is provided to third parties in violation of laws and regulations).

Article 6 (Organization and Structure)
    The Company shall appoint a Personal Information Protection Manager to ensure the proper management of personal information.

    The Company shall provide training to directors and employees on the protection of personal information and proper management methods, ensuring the proper handling of personal information in daily operations.

Article 7 (Revision of the Policy)
The Company may change the content of this Privacy Policy as necessary. In such cases, the latest content will be promptly notified within the application of this service. The revised content shall take effect from the time it is posted on this application by the Company.

Article 8 (Contact)
If users wish to inquire about or correct their personal information, or have any inquiries regarding the above privacy policy, please contact the following:
